Third-party components
----------------------

The terms above cover this project's own code only. app-tail statically links
open-source Go modules that remain under their own licenses. Their full texts
are reproduced in internal/licenses/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, which ships as
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt beside every released binary, inside App-Tail.app, and
is embedded in the binary itself:

    app-tail licenses

Regenerate that file after any dependency change with scripts/licenses.sh; the
ship gate fails if it is stale.

Two components are not Go modules and carry their own terms:

  * wintun.dll, shipped in the Windows archive, is proprietary software from
    WireGuard LLC. It is redistributed unmodified, with its license text as
    WINTUN-LICENSE.txt beside it. See https://www.wintun.net/.

  * OpenVPN, used for OpenVPN connections on macOS and Linux, is GPL-2.0 and is
    installed separately by the user or by setup.sh. app-tail runs it as a
    subprocess and links no part of it.
